    {
      "title": "A slow email makes a slow checkout",
      "narrative": "After the card is charged and the paid order is saved, Place order sends the receipt to Email provider and waits until it is accepted. The email client tries up to 3 times, all inside the shopper's request, and the confirmation page waits for it. So a slow or failing Email provider slows every checkout, at a point where the payment and the order are already done.",
